{"id":"c6ace29e12d6a2ff","group":"58","path":"58/batch03/58-thm-polar-decomposition.md","title":"Polar Decomposition","display":"thm-polar-decomposition — Polar Decomposition","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-polar-decomposition","aliases":["58-thm-polar-decomposition"],"display":"thm-polar-decomposition — Polar Decomposition","depends_on":["[[../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md]]","[[58-df-bounded-operator]]","[[../batch12/58-df-adjoint.md]]","[[../batch17/58-df-partial-isometry.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-polar-decomposition"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-polar-decomposition</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-polar-decomposition — Polar Decomposition"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"b70ce791d5b1a19b\" href=\"?note=b70ce791d5b1a19b\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md\">../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"2ad9c248fe18df37\" href=\"?note=2ad9c248fe18df37\" title=\"58-df-bounded-operator\">58-df-bounded-operator</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"200eacd293b1282b\" href=\"?note=200eacd293b1282b\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-adjoint.md\">../batch12/58-df-adjoint.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"0e9a7e858e6fae46\" href=\"?note=0e9a7e858e6fae46\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-partial-isometry.md\">../batch17/58-df-partial-isometry.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H,K,T,T^\\ast,A,P,U,B_H,B_K,k,+_H,\\odot_H,+_K,\\odot_K,Z,N_T\\in V\">\\(H,K,T,T^\\ast,A,P,U,B_H,B_K,k,+_H,\\odot_H,+_K,\\odot_K,Z,N_T\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"0_k,0_H,0_K\">\\(0_k,0_H,0_K\\)</span> are the additive identities determined by the selected field and Hilbert structures</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{BoundedOperatorStructure}_S\\subseteq V^{10}\">\\(\\mathrm{BoundedOperatorStructure}_S\\subseteq V^{10}\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{AdjointStructure}_S\\subseteq V^{11}\">\\(\\mathrm{AdjointStructure}_S\\subseteq V^{11}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PartialIsometry}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{PartialIsometry}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PositiveSquareRootStructure}_S\\subseteq V^7\">\\(\\mathrm{PositiveSquareRootStructure}_S\\subseteq V^7\\)</span> is the selected-structure predicate defined below</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}positive\\text{-}square\\text{-}root\\text{-}selected}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{PositiveSquareRootStructure}_S(P,A,H,B_H,k,+_H,\\odot_H)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,B_H,k,+_H,\\odot_H)\n\\land\\mathrm{BoundedOperatorStructure}_S\n(P;H,\\nu_{B_H},+_H,\\odot_H;H,\\nu_{B_H},+_H,\\odot_H;k)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land A=\\{\\langle x,P(P(x))\\rangle:x\\in H\\}\n\\land\\forall x,y\\in H\\;(B_H(P(x),y)=B_H(x,P(y)))\n\\land\\forall x\\in H\\;(B_H(P(x),x)\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}positive\\text{-}square\\text{-}root\\text{-}selected}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{PositiveSquareRootStructure}_S(P,A,H,B_H,k,+_H,\\odot_H)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,B_H,k,+_H,\\odot_H)\n\\land\\mathrm{BoundedOperatorStructure}_S\n(P;H,\\nu_{B_H},+_H,\\odot_H;H,\\nu_{B_H},+_H,\\odot_H;k)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land A=\\{\\langle x,P(P(x))\\rangle:x\\in H\\}\n\\land\\forall x,y\\in H\\;(B_H(P(x),y)=B_H(x,P(y)))\n\\land\\forall x\\in H\\;(B_H(P(x),x)\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}polar\\text{-}decomposition}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,B_H,k,+_H,\\odot_H)\n\\land\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(K,B_K,k,+_K,\\odot_K)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\mathrm{BoundedOperatorStructure}_S\n(T;H,\\nu_{B_H},+_H,\\odot_H;K,\\nu_{B_K},+_K,\\odot_K;k)\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\exists!(T^\\ast,A,P,U,Z,N_T)\\in V^6\\;\\Bigl[\n\\mathrm{AdjointStructure}_S\n(T,T^\\ast,H,B_H,K,B_K,k,+_H,\\odot_H,+_K,\\odot_K)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land A=\\{\\langle x,T^\\ast(T(x))\\rangle:x\\in H\\}\n\\land\\mathrm{PositiveSquareRootStructure}_S(P,A,H,B_H,k,+_H,\\odot_H)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\mathrm{PartialIsometry}_S(U,H,K)\n\\land\\mathrm{BoundedOperatorStructure}_S\n(U;H,\\nu_{B_H},+_H,\\odot_H;K,\\nu_{B_K},+_K,\\odot_K;k)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land Z=\\{x\\in H:T(x)=0_K\\}\n\\land N_T=\\{x\\in H:\\forall z\\in Z\\;(B_H(x,z)=0_k)\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\{x\\in H:U(x)=0_K\\}=Z\n\\land\\forall x,y\\in N_T\\;(B_K(U(x),U(y))=B_H(x,y))\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land T=\\{\\langle x,U(P(x))\\rangle:x\\in H\\}\n\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}polar\\text{-}decomposition}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,B_H,k,+_H,\\odot_H)\n\\land\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(K,B_K,k,+_K,\\odot_K)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\mathrm{BoundedOperatorStructure}_S\n(T;H,\\nu_{B_H},+_H,\\odot_H;K,\\nu_{B_K},+_K,\\odot_K;k)\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\exists!(T^\\ast,A,P,U,Z,N_T)\\in V^6\\;\\Bigl[\n\\mathrm{AdjointStructure}_S\n(T,T^\\ast,H,B_H,K,B_K,k,+_H,\\odot_H,+_K,\\odot_K)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land A=\\{\\langle x,T^\\ast(T(x))\\rangle:x\\in H\\}\n\\land\\mathrm{PositiveSquareRootStructure}_S(P,A,H,B_H,k,+_H,\\odot_H)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\mathrm{PartialIsometry}_S(U,H,K)\n\\land\\mathrm{BoundedOperatorStructure}_S\n(U;H,\\nu_{B_H},+_H,\\odot_H;K,\\nu_{B_K},+_K,\\odot_K;k)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land Z=\\{x\\in H:T(x)=0_K\\}\n\\land N_T=\\{x\\in H:\\forall z\\in Z\\;(B_H(x,z)=0_k)\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\{x\\in H:U(x)=0_K\\}=Z\n\\land\\forall x,y\\in N_T\\;(B_K(U(x),U(y))=B_H(x,y))\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land T=\\{\\langle x,U(P(x))\\rangle:x\\in H\\}\n\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Polar decomposition: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T=U|T|\">\\(T=U|T|\\)</span> with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|T|=(T^*T)^{1/2}\">\\(|T|=(T^*T)^{1/2}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"U\">\\(U\\)</span> the uniquely normalized phase.</li>\n<li>The adjoint, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T^*T\">\\(T^*T\\)</span>, positive square root, factorization, kernel, and selected inner-product isometry are all represented by set graphs or sourced predicates.  No partial global adjoint or square-root operator remains.</li>\n<li>The kernel normalization fixes <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"U\">\\(U\\)</span> on all of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H\">\\(H\\)</span>; the usual range-closure identities follow from these clauses and are not needed as extra uniqueness assumptions.</li>\n<li>Analogous to complex number polar form <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"z = e^{i\\theta} |z|\">\\(z = e^{i\\theta} |z|\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"b70ce791d5b1a19b","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-bounded-operator","status":"resolved","id":"2ad9c248fe18df37","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-bounded-operator]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-adjoint.md","status":"resolved","id":"200eacd293b1282b","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-adjoint.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch17/58-df-partial-isometry.md","status":"resolved","id":"0e9a7e858e6fae46","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch17/58-df-partial-isometry.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"H,K,T,T^\\ast,A,P,U,B_H,B_K,k,+_H,\\odot_H,+_K,\\odot_K,Z,N_T\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"0_k,0_H,0_K","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{BoundedOperatorStructure}_S\\subseteq V^{10}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{AdjointStructure}_S\\subseteq V^{11}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{PartialIsometry}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{PositiveSquareRootStructure}_S\\subseteq V^7","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{df\\text{-}positive\\text{-}square\\text{-}root\\text{-}selected}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{PositiveSquareRootStructure}_S(P,A,H,B_H,k,+_H,\\odot_H)\\\\\n&\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,B_H,k,+_H,\\odot_H)\n\\land\\mathrm{BoundedOperatorStructure}_S\n(P;H,\\nu_{B_H},+_H,\\odot_H;H,\\nu_{B_H},+_H,\\odot_H;k)\\\\\n&\\qquad\\land A=\\{\\langle x,P(P(x))\\rangle:x\\in H\\}\n\\land\\forall x,y\\in H\\;(B_H(P(x),y)=B_H(x,P(y)))\n\\land\\forall x\\in H\\;(B_H(P(x),x)\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}polar\\text{-}decomposition}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,B_H,k,+_H,\\odot_H)\n\\land\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(K,B_K,k,+_K,\\odot_K)\\\\\n&\\quad\\land\\mathrm{BoundedOperatorStructure}_S\n(T;H,\\nu_{B_H},+_H,\\odot_H;K,\\nu_{B_K},+_K,\\odot_K;k)\\\\\n&\\to\\exists!(T^\\ast,A,P,U,Z,N_T)\\in V^6\\;\\Bigl[\n\\mathrm{AdjointStructure}_S\n(T,T^\\ast,H,B_H,K,B_K,k,+_H,\\odot_H,+_K,\\odot_K)\\\\\n&\\qquad\\land A=\\{\\langle x,T^\\ast(T(x))\\rangle:x\\in H\\}\n\\land\\mathrm{PositiveSquareRootStructure}_S(P,A,H,B_H,k,+_H,\\odot_H)\\\\\n&\\qquad\\land\\mathrm{PartialIsometry}_S(U,H,K)\n\\land\\mathrm{BoundedOperatorStructure}_S\n(U;H,\\nu_{B_H},+_H,\\odot_H;K,\\nu_{B_K},+_K,\\odot_K;k)\\\\\n&\\qquad\\land Z=\\{x\\in H:T(x)=0_K\\}\n\\land N_T=\\{x\\in H:\\forall z\\in Z\\;(B_H(x,z)=0_k)\\}\\\\\n&\\qquad\\land\\{x\\in H:U(x)=0_K\\}=Z\n\\land\\forall x,y\\in N_T\\;(B_K(U(x),U(y))=B_H(x,y))\\\\\n&\\qquad\\land T=\\{\\langle x,U(P(x))\\rangle:x\\in H\\}\n\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"T=U|T|","display":false},{"tex":"|T|=(T^*T)^{1/2}","display":false},{"tex":"U","display":false},{"tex":"T^*T","display":false},{"tex":"U","display":false},{"tex":"H","display":false},{"tex":"z = e^{i\\theta} |z|","display":false}],"bytes":3004,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc7